{
  "assessment": "The source provides a clear quantitative cluster: trapped-atom exponential decay versus lattice hold time for the 3D and 1D lattices, with fitted lifetimes of 54 ms and 220 ms, respectively. The source reports the hold-time domain (excluding t_hold < 75 ms), the readout (number of trapped atoms), and the exponential decay model. The reviewer figure evidence confirms that the displayed fit segments pass through 100, 200, and 300 ms, but does not provide raw data points or uncertainties. The source does not report the initial atom number or the exact fit equation parameters beyond the lifetimes, so the quantitative form is limited to the exponential decay with the reported lifetimes. The case is authoring-ready because it supports a numeric control (hold time), a numeric readout (atom number), a quantitative mechanism (exponential decay), and an objective response within an explicit domain.",
